cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Certified worst-case bounds for ligand-receptor statistics over
  segmentation uncertainty in spatial transcriptomics
message: >-
  If you use this code or the certified-bound construction, please cite the
  accompanying manuscript and this repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Amy
    family-names: Wang
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-13"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amywang2010/lr-certificates"
abstract: >-
  Per-contrast intervals for ligand-receptor statistics in spatial
  transcriptomics, valid over an explicit uncertainty set of molecule-to-cell
  assignments (boundary-local reassignment with capacity constraints, mask
  erosion/dilation, and a parameterised donor radius). A direction is certified only
  when both bounds exclude zero and a permutation null matched to the
  worst-case layer confirms it; everything else is reported as
  non-identifiable. Evaluated on three public Xenium sections spanning two
  panel densities and two tumor types.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - cell-cell communication
  - segmentation uncertainty
  - certified bounds
  - ligand-receptor
